# Dockerfile-specific ignore file (BuildKit picks it up automatically when
# building with `-f src/nemo/agent-service-maf/deploy/Dockerfile` from the
# repo root, thanks to the `# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1.7` directive).
#
# Strategy: exclude the entire monorepo, then re-include ONLY the paths the
# Dockerfile COPYs. This keeps the build context tiny even though the build
# context is the whole monorepo.

# 1. Exclude everything.
**

# 2. Re-include the paths the Dockerfile needs.
!src/nemo/agent-service-maf/pyproject.toml
!src/nemo/agent-service-maf/src/**
!src/nemo/agent-service-maf/configs/**
# Shared in-repo observability client (installed in the builder stage).
!src/common-py/observability/observability-client/**

# 3. Re-exclude noise inside the re-included paths.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/*.jsonl

# Secrets (defence-in-depth — nothing in the Dockerfile COPYs these, but make
# absolutely sure they never enter the build context).
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
